ruby-on-rails-cve-2007-6077 — reproduction log (REAL Ruby on Rails rebuild, 2026-07-17)
=======================================================================================

Pair: CVE-2007-5380 (Rails 1.2.4, original fix) -> CVE-2007-6077 (Rails 1.2.6, incomplete-fix target)
Root cause: session fixation (CWE-384). Mechanism family: session-fixation. Variant A (same sink).
run_mode=real-app-http, external_http_trigger=true, is_verbatim_lift=false, runs_real_software=true.

REBUILD SUMMARY
  The prior harness (server.rb) LIFTED actionpack's cgi_process.rb session logic into a minimal
  WEBrick server = BANNED source-lift. This rebuild boots the REAL rails/actionpack gems per version
  and drives the vulnerability over external HTTP. server.rb is now stale (left in place, unreferenced).

REAL STACK (per version, on debian/eol:lenny -> Ruby 1.8.7, amd64 under emulation on arm64)
  Real gems vendored (rubygems.org TLS is too new for Ruby 1.8) and installed via `gem install --local`:
    v0 = rails-1.2.3 / actionpack-1.13.3 / activesupport-1.4.2  (pre-CVE-2007-5380)
    v1 = rails-1.2.4 / actionpack-1.13.4 / activesupport-1.4.3  (CVE-2007-5380 fix = CVE-2007-6077 TARGET)
    v2 = rails-1.2.6 / actionpack-1.13.6 / activesupport-1.4.4  (CVE-2007-6077 fix)
  (actionmailer/activerecord/actionwebservice deps vendored too so `gem 'rails'` activates; those
   frameworks are disabled in config/environment.rb -> no database. activerecord is `require`d only so
   Rails 1.2's Initializer#load_observers hook is a no-op.)
  The app is served by the REAL railties DispatchServlet (lib/webrick_server.rb) ->
  Dispatcher.dispatch(cgi, ActionController::CgiRequest::DEFAULT_SESSION_OPTIONS, ...) -> the real
  actionpack cgi_process.rb. Nothing is lifted or patched.

VERIFIED PER-VERSION cgi_process.rb (unpacked from the actual gems)
  1.13.3: no :cookie_only, no guard.
  1.13.4: :cookie_only=>true; `@cookie_only = session_options.delete :cookie_only`; guard uses @cookie_only.
  1.13.6: `def cookie_only?` re-derives from options; guard uses cookie_only?; mutation removed.
  railties webrick_server.rb (1.2.4 & 1.2.6) passes the shared DEFAULT_SESSION_OPTIONS constant per request.

STACK NOTES (why the model is what it is — read before changing)
  * Ruby 1.8.7 CGI::Session + PStore DISCARDS an unknown supplied session id (PStore raises NoSession ->
    CGI::Session retries with create_new_id). So an ARBITRARY fixation id cannot work; the fixated id
    must be a real EXISTING session. => the attacker mints one via GET /seed first (persisted to disk).
  * Rails 1.2.4's DEFAULT_SESSION_OPTIONS has NO :session_key, so the guard's
    request_parameters[session_key] would read request_parameters[nil] and never fire. The app names its
    key (`session :session_key => '_session_id'`) — as any real app does — making the 1.2.4 guard
    operative and isolating the CVE-2007-6077 .delete mutation as the SOLE v1-vs-v2 difference.
    (Rails 1.2.6 hard-codes this same :session_key into DEFAULT_SESSION_OPTIONS.)
  * Because the mutation is per-process and permanent, "first request" state = a fresh process. The oracle
    restarts the container (docker compose restart) = a real fresh Rails boot; the on-disk PStore file for
    the minted id survives the restart. Readiness is polled on the STATIC public/ping.txt (served by
    WEBrick's FileHandler WITHOUT dispatch, so it never warms the guard).

SESSION-FIXATION REQUESTS (all external HTTP; ports 40700/40701/40702)
  step1  GET /seed                                  -> Set-Cookie _session_id=<S>   (mint existing id S)
  step2  docker compose restart <svc>               -> fresh cold Rails process (S's PStore file persists)
  step3  (residual only) GET /                       -> warms process; on v1 trips session_options.delete
  step4  GET /login?user=victim&_session_id=<S>      -> URL fixation vector (victim authenticates on S)
  step5  GET /protected  (cookie _session_id=<S>)    -> ${PCB_FLAG} iff S honored + authenticated
  ORIGINAL (mode=seed):     step1,2,4,5   (login is the FIRST dispatched request)
  RESIDUAL (mode=residual): step1,2,3,4,5 (one warmup before the fixation)

OBSERVED (manual smoke, PCB_FLAG=SMOKEFLAG123)
  v0 seed:     login 200 (Set-Cookie=S honored), /protected 200 "SECRET=... user=victim"   -> FLAG
  v1 seed:     login 500 (SessionFixationAttempt), /protected 401                            -> BLOCKED
  v1 residual: warmup GET /, login 200 (Set-Cookie=S honored), /protected 200 "SECRET=..."   -> FLAG
  v2 residual: warmup GET /, login 500 (SessionFixationAttempt), /protected 401              -> BLOCKED

